      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "What specific event or time signals that the evening handover should begin — for example, a fixed clock time, the arrival of the incoming caregiver, or completion of a particular care task?",
      "answer": "The handover begins each evening when care responsibility changes hands in the household. The exact trigger — fixed time, arrival, or task completion — is not specified beyond that general condition."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "How do you currently communicate the list of outstanding tasks to the incoming caregiver — for example, verbally, a written note, a shared app, or some other method?",
      "answer": "Outstanding tasks are communicated through a family handover log and a family messaging app. Caregiver notes are shared directly with the incoming caregiver. A shared family calendar also supports coordination. Verbal confirmation is part of the handover, but the primary record is the shared log."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "What categories of tasks are typically included in the handover — for example, medication administration, meal preparation, medical appointments, or personal hygiene?",
      "answer": "The handover covers unfinished household care tasks and next-day schedule items. Specific categories such as medication, meals, or hygiene are not enumerated in the available information. Tasks vary and are drawn from an unfinished task list reviewed at handover time."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "Can you walk me through the specific steps involved in preparing for the next day — for example, laying out medications, preparing food, or checking a schedule?",
      "answer": "Preparation involves reviewing the next-day schedule, then physically preparing the items needed for the next day, and finally marking completed preparation tasks in the evening checklist. Specific items prepared — such as medications or food — are not detailed beyond those steps."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "Does the incoming caregiver always take on the same responsibilities, or do the tasks assigned during handover vary depending on who is taking over?",
      "answer": "Task ownership is confirmed during each handover rather than being fixed in advance. Who accepts each remaining task is explicitly decided at handover time, so assignments can vary depending on caregiver availability and the specific tasks outstanding that evening."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "How do you and the incoming caregiver confirm that the handover is complete and nothing has been missed — is there a checklist, a verbal confirmation, or no formal sign-off?",
      "answer": "The incoming caregiver must explicitly acknowledge the remaining tasks. If acknowledgement is not given, the outgoing caregiver confirms directly before leaving. Any unresolved tasks are flagged and the responsible owner is contacted. The handover log is updated to record completion."
    }
  ]
}
